  "metaDescription": "Four Indonesian police generals, including former officials, have been named suspects in an illegal wiretapping case targeting President Prabowo Subianto.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Four high-ranking police officers, including a former National Police Chief, have been named suspects in the illegal wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto.",
    "Bareskrim Polri confirmed investigations are ongoing, with suspects facing potential 10-year prison terms and upcoming ethics hearings.",
    "Parliamentary leaders have directed the House Commission III to oversee the legal proceedings surrounding these allegations."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) Bareskrim has named four high-ranking police generals as suspects regarding an illegal wiretapping case involving President Prabowo Subianto. Among those implicated are former National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo and Irjen Slamet Uliandi. Reports indicate the wiretapping was conducted without following legal protocols, leading to allegations of data tampering. Officials have clarified that no dedicated facility was established for the act, while some public officials have characterized the gravity of the situation as reaching the level of treason. In response to the unfolding investigation, the House of Representatives leadership, led by Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, has formally requested that Commission III monitor the case closely. Meanwhile, the suspects are expected to face both criminal prosecution and internal police ethics hearings as investigations proceed.",
